"The Architect": "I've never let a thought pass without thinking about it before..."
You watch as the architect takes one more deep breath and closes their eyes, accepting the thought and letting it pass,  the thoughts coming out of the architect's head aren't as loud, and they begin to dissipate as soon as they come to form.
You and the architect sit and breathe, taking more time with each breath to pause and accept each thought that has come through your mind.
"The Architect": "Where did you learn that? What was that? It couldn't have just been because of the breathing could it?"
- It's called mindfulness
- That was a breif meditation
- Breathing techniques can help in stressful situations
